      Moreover,chemical structure alone cannot fully represent polymers in some cases,as their properties are regulated by multiple factors mentioned        
      above.An ideal framework needs to possess a mechanism forintegrating supplementary conditions.In some studies,conditions such as molecular weight or   
      external factors are encoded as special tokens and concatenated with SMILES39.This approach implicitly encodes the relationship between conditions and 
      polymer structures, which may constrain the model's understanding of complex chemical dependencies.Therefore,it is crucial to develop a unified deep   
      learn-ing framework that explicitly models both the intrinsic periodicity of polymers and their behavior under various conditions,thereby accurately   
      capturing complex chemical interactions.                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                             
      Motivated by the challenges above,we propose the periodicityawaregraph transformer (PerioGT),aunified deep learning framework for polymers. Our        
      contributions are as follows: (1) We introduce a chemical knowledge-driven sampling module,named periodicity augmentation(PA),serving as a periodic    
      prior.(2)We proposea PA-based contrastive learning pre-training,which integrates the periodic prior to enhance the model's ability to recognize and    
      encode periodic patterns.(3)A periodicity prompt-guided fine-tuning(PGFT) strategy is employed, introducing periodic prompts based on PA in fine-tuning
      to better leverage the knowledge learned in pre-training.(4) To establish a unified deep learning framework for polymers,we propose a modular graph    
      augmentation strategy (named PolymerGraph) that explicitly encodes the relationships between additional information and polymers into the graph,       
      enabling relational modeling.(5) As a case study,the proposed model is further applied to the screening of antimicrobial polymers,and we successfully  
      screened 25 polymers with antimicrobial activity,two of which show excellent antimicrobial activity against methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus
      (MRSA).                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                                             
      # Results                                                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                                             
      # Model overview                                                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                                                             
      To explicitly model the periodicity and exploit the large amount of unlabeled data, we propose a contrastive learning strategy, where PA,together with 
      random masking,generates multiple equivalent fragments from the same polymer as positives,while fragments from different polymers serve as negatives   
      (Fig.la).PA provides different views ofthe same polymer,including different orders of arrangement and different degrees of polymerization(Fig.Ib).Our  
      approach enables the modelto capture periodicpatterns by learning invariant representations across fragments derived from the same polymer and         
      explicitly guiding it to align structurally distinct fragments that encode similar semantic information.Besides,previous SSL models rely on masked     
      language modeling,which captures local dependencies in chemistry but is limited in global modeling43.Contrastive learning is widely used to promote    
      global structural understanding by aligning semantically similar inputs43-45. We therefore hypothesize that,byintroducing the periodicity prior,our    
      method further enhances the global representation of polymers.                                                                                         
                                                                                                                                                             
