      The SMILES of RU was first converted into a molecular graph using RDKit and the DGL package,with atomic and bond features summarizedin                 
      SupplementaryTables 6and 7.For clarity,we denote the graph as $G _ { 0 } = ( V _ { 0 } , E _ { 0 } )$ ， where $V _ { 0 } = \{ v _ { i } \} _ { i \in [
      1 , N _ { v } ] }$ and $E _ { 0 } = \{ e _ { i , j } \} _ { i , j \in [ 1 , N _ { v } ] }$ are nodes (atoms)and edges (bonds),respectively. $G _ { 0 }$
      is furthertransformed into a line graph $\hat { G } = ( \hat { V } , \hat { E } )$ with the following steps: (1) node creation: for each $e _ { i , j }
      \in E _ { 0 } ,$ create acorresponding node $\hat { v } _ { i , j } \in \hat { V }$ and (2) edge creation: two nodes in $\hat { V }$ are connected by  
      an edge in $\hat { E }$ if and only if the corresponding two edges in $G _ { 0 }$ share a common vertex.The features of $\hat { v } _ { i , j }$ are   
      initialized to $\mathbf { h } _ { v _ { i , j } } \in \mathbb { R } ^ { d }$ ,which is formulated as:                                                  
                                                                                                                                                             
