      repeating unit $- \mathtt { A } -$ where $V _ { A }$ represents atoms and $E _ { A }$ represent bonds. These methods ignore chain-level connectivity   
      [15,18, 37]. They apply mean/sum aggregation on this monomer graph and assume the learned embedding $h _ { \theta } ( G )$ will generalize to arbitrary
      repeat size $n$ ,which we found fails: Model-wise, mean erases all size information and sum grows unbounded with $n$ .Data-wise,real polymers include  
      both intra-monomer and inter-monomer connections, while the previous monomer graph captures only the former.                                           
                                                                                                                                                             
