      Repetition INvariance) combines algorithm alignment with repeat-unit augmentation to achieve repetition-invariant representation learning. The core    
      insight is to align message passing with Maximum Spanning Tree (MST) construction via Prim's algorithm, which enjoys inherent size-generalization      
      through dynamic programming recurrence. **Max-Aggregation GNN**: The node update uses element-wise maximum over incoming messages: h_v^(ℓ) = h_v^(ℓ-1) 
      + U^(ℓ)(h_v^(ℓ-1), max_{u∈N(v)} M^(ℓ)(h_u^(ℓ-1), e_uv)). This selects the single most informative incoming message, unlike sum/mean which blend all    
      neighbors. The additive residual ensures nodes not chosen in the greedy step remain unchanged, mirroring Prim's algorithm. **L1 Sparsity Penalty**:    
      Added to message and update network parameters to suppress non-dominant pathways, encouraging a sparse MST-like backbone: L_total = L_task +           
      λ∑(‖θ_M^(ℓ)‖_1 + ‖θ_U^(ℓ)‖_1). **Repeat-Unit Augmentation**: Construct polymer graphs G^(n) by chaining n repeating units with polymerization points.  
