      where U_Coul is the electrostatic component and ΔU is a learned correction. CELLI comprises four key components: (1) Environment Embedding: A          
      multi-layer perceptron MLP_R predicts per-edge contributions to electronegativity (χ̃_ij) and optionally hardness (J̃_ij^R) from latent scalar features  
      x_ij^l encoding many-body information. The electronegativity χ_i = f·Σ_k χ̃_ik is computed by summing edge contributions with a species-invariant       
      learnable factor f. (2) Species Embedding: Encodes particle species to environmentally independent hardness contributions J̃_i^Z. The particle hardness 
      J_i = σ_+(J̃_i^Z, Σ_j J̃_ij^R) uses a generalized softplus activation σ_+ to ensure positivity. Charge radii γ_i are based on covalent radii with learned
      species-dependent scaling. (3) Charge Equilibration (Qeq): Takes environment-dependent electronegativities, species/environment-dependent hardnesses,  
      and species-dependent charge radii to predict partial charges Q and coulombic potential. Optionally employs Smooth Particle Mesh for periodic systems. 
      (4) Charge Embedding and Feature Update: MLP_Q generates charge-dependent features y_ij from equilibrated charges and species embeddings, which MLP_x  
