      Bartosh', 'Mikkel N. Schmidt', 'Christian A. Naesseth'], 'summary': 'We introduce Equivariant Neural Diffusion (END), a novel diffusion model for      
      molecule generation in 3D that is equivariant to Euclidean transformations. Compared to current state-of-the-art equivariant diffusion models, the key 
      innovation in END lies in its learnable forward process for enhanced generative modelling. Rather than pre-specified, the forward process is           
      parameterized through a time- and data-dependent transformation that is equivariant to rigid transformations. Through a series of experiments on       
      standard molecule generation benchmarks, we demonstrate the competitive performance of END compared to several strong baselines for both unconditional 
