      small dataset is randomly sampled from the large training dataset.Forvalidation and test datasets,we follow the splitting strategy reported in the     
      previous literature for ISOl7 (ref.1l).This makes it convenient for us to evaluate the effectiveness of GPIP.We train the                              
                                                                                                                                                             
      GNN with AdamW47 optimizer,and the hyperparameters are provided in Supplementary Table 7.                                                              
                                                                                                                                                             
      Liquid water with PBCs.We benchmark different models with training datasets with the sizes of 95O for DimeNet and GemNet-T and 9,500 for SchNet and use
      the remaining 1O,OoO structures for testing. We perform five simulations of 5oo ps by initializing from five randomly sampled testing                  
      configurations,witha time step of1fs,atthetemperature of3oo K.The other experimental settings are the same as in ref.37.                               
                                                                                                                                                             
      Electrolyte solutions with PBCs.The training, validation and test sets contain 240,60and 500 configurations,respectively.Fortraining hyperparameters,we
