      Zhao', 'Junbin Gao'], 'summary': "Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) have emerged as one of the leading approaches for machine learning on graph-structured  
      data. Despite their great success, critical computational challenges such as over-smoothing, over-squashing, and limited expressive power continue to  
      impact the performance of GNNs. In this study, inspired from the time-reversal principle commonly utilized in classical and quantum physics, we reverse
      the time direction of the graph heat equation. The resulted reversing process yields a class of high pass filtering functions that enhance the         
      sharpness of graph node features. Leveraging this concept, we introduce the Multi-Scaled Heat Kernel based GNN (MHKG) by amalgamating diverse filtering
