      bonds in QM9 molecules, optimizing radical fragments at B3LYP/6-31G(2df,p) level.', 'result': 'On QM9, X2-GNN achieves 6.76 meV MAE for internal energy
      U_0, competitive with baselines (SchNet: 14 meV, DimeNet++: 6.32 meV, Allegro: 4.9 meV, Equiformer: 7.32 meV). The key result is generalization to     
