      ·Although many constructive proofs of the Kolmogorov-Arnold representation theorem indicate that the iner functions $\phi _ { q , p }$ in equation 1   
      are highly non-smooth [41, 42], KAN opts for smooth functions as pre-activation functions ${ \boldsymbol { \phi } _ { j , i } ^ { ( l ) } }$           
