      messages = self.message_mlp(torch.cat([h[src], h[dst]], dim=-1))\n        \n        # Aggregate messages\n        aggr = torch.zeros_like(h)\n         
      aggr.scatter_add_(0, dst.unsqueeze(-1).expand(-1, self.hidden_dim), messages)\n        \n        # SSM update: H^(k+1)⊤ = ΛH^(k)⊤ + BX^(k)⊤\n        # 
      Here X^(k) is the aggregated messages\n        h_new = torch.matmul(h, self.Lambda.T) + torch.matmul(aggr, self.B.T)\n        \n        return         
      self.norm(h_new)\n```\n\n### 3.4 Complete PolyKAN-SSM Architecture\n```python\nclass PolyKANSSM(nn.Module):\n    """\n    PolyKAN-SSM: Integrating     
      Fourier-KAN, GNN-SSM, and Non-covalent edges.\n    \n    Architecture:\n    1. Node/Edge embedding with Fourier-KAN\n    2. 4 GNN-SSM layers for       
      message passing with gradient control\n    3. Attention-based pooling for intensive property (Tg)\n    4. MLP head with Fourier-KAN activations\n      
      """\n    def __init__(self, node_dim, edge_dim, hidden_dim=256, num_layers=4, num_heads=4):\n        super().__init__()\n        \n        # Node/Edge 
      embedding\n        self.node_embed = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(node_dim, hidden_dim),\n            FourierKANLayer(hidden_dim, hidden_dim, 
      num_frequencies=8)\n        )\n        self.edge_embed = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(edge_dim, hidden_dim),\n                                
      FourierKANLayer(hidden_dim, hidden_dim, num_frequencies=8)\n        )\n        \n        # GNN-SSM layers\n        self.ssm_layers = nn.ModuleList([\n 
      GNNSSMLayer(hidden_dim, num_heads, spectral_radius=0.99)\n            for _ in range(num_layers)\n        ])\n        \n        # Attention-based      
      pooling (validated in Day 4)\n        self.attention_pool = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(hidden_dim, hidden_dim),\n                           
      FourierKANLayer(hidden_dim, 1, num_frequencies=8)\n        )\n        \n        # Prediction head\n        self.head = nn.Sequential(\n                
      nn.Linear(hidden_dim, hidden_dim),\n            FourierKANLayer(hidden_dim, hidden_dim, num_frequencies=8),\n            nn.Dropout(0.1),\n            
      nn.Linear(hidden_dim, 1)\n        )\n        \n    def forward(self, batch):\n        # Embed nodes and edges\n        h = self.node_embed(batch.x)\n  
      edge_attr = self.edge_embed(batch.edge_attr)\n        \n        # GNN-SSM layers\n        for ssm_layer in self.ssm_layers:\n            h =           
      ssm_layer(h, batch.edge_index, edge_attr)\n        \n        # Attention-based pooling for intensive property\n        attn_weights =                  
      self.attention_pool(h)  # [num_nodes, 1]\n        attn_weights = torch.softmax(attn_weights, dim=0)\n        \n        # Graph-level representation\n  
      graph_repr = (h * attn_weights).sum(dim=0, keepdim=True)  # [1, hidden_dim]\n        \n        # Predict Tg\n        out = self.head(graph_repr)\n     
      return out.squeeze()\n```\n\n## 4. Experimental Strategy\n\n### 4.1 Data Processing\n1. Load Tg dataset (7170 samples)\n2. For each SMILES:\n   -      
      Generate 3D conformer with RDKit (ETKDG, max 1 conformer)\n   - If conformer generation succeeds:\n     - Extract atom positions\n     - Build covalent
      edges from bonds\n     - Build non-covalent edges (distance < 5Å, excluding covalent)\n   - If conformer generation fails:\n     - Use 2D graph with   
      shortest path distances as proxy\n3. Node features: atom type (one-hot), degree, hybridization, aromaticity, formal charge, is_in_ring\n4. Edge        
      features: bond type (one-hot), conjugated, in_ring, distance encoding (Gaussian basis)\n\n### 4.2 Training\n- Optimizer: AdamW (lr=1e-3,               
      weight_decay=1e-4)\n- Scheduler: ReduceLROnPlateau (patience=10, factor=0.5)\n- Loss: MSE\n- Batch size: 32\n- Early stopping: patience=30 on          
      validation RMSE\n- Max epochs: 500\n- 5 random seeds for ensemble\n\n### 4.3 Evaluation\n- Metric: RMSE on test set\n- Compare against: SOTA 30.8      
      (PerioGT), current best 34.14 (Day 1)\n- Target: Beat SOTA 30.8\n\n## 5. Diagnostic Analysis\n\n### 5.1 Gradient Flow Analysis\n- Monitor layer-wise   
      Jacobian eigenvalues\n- Track Dirichlet energy evolution\n- Compare with vanilla GNN baseline\n\n### 5.2 Overfitting Analysis\n- Track train vs        
      validation loss curves\n- Compare with Day 4 results (train ~12-17, val ~35-37)\n- Analyze if GNN-SSM reduces the gap\n\n### 5.3 Ablation Studies\n1.  
      PolyKAN-SSM (full) vs without Fourier-KAN (use GELU)\n2. PolyKAN-SSM vs without GNN-SSM (use standard GIN)\n3. PolyKAN-SSM vs without non-covalent     
      edges\n4. Spectral radius ablation (0.9, 0.95, 0.99, 1.0)\n\n### 5.4 Feature Visualization\n- t-SNE of learned representations\n- Attention weights    
      visualization\n- Non-covalent edge importance\n\n## 6. Constraints\n- Libraries: PyTorch, PyTorch Geometric, RDKit\n- Data: Only Tg dataset (no        
      pre-training on PI1M)\n- Hardware: 2x 2080Ti\n\n## 7. Expected Output\n- src/day6_polykanssm/model.py - Model implementation\n-                        
