      200°C, surpassing commercial polymers by 11× and enabling high-temperature electrostatic capacitors without cooling systems.'}, {'id': 'mem_035',      
      'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper demonstrates that pre-trained graph neural network (GNN) property predictors can be directly inverted via  
      gradient ascent on constrained molecular graph representations to generate diverse molecules with targeted electronic or physicochemical properties,   
      without any additional training.'}, {'id': 'mem_036', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper proposes Graph Convolutional Policy Network (GCPN), a
      reinforcement learning framework for goal-directed molecular graph generation that combines graph representation, policy gradient optimization, and    
      adversarial training to directly optimize molecular properties while ensuring chemical validity and realism.'}, {'id': 'mem_037', 'type': 'knowledge', 
      'abstract': 'The paper proposes Kolmogorov–Arnold Graph Neural Networks (KA-GNNs), which fully integrate Fourier-series-based KAN modules into all core
      GNN components—node embedding, message passing, and readout—achieving state-of-the-art accuracy, computational efficiency, and interpretability on     
      molecular property prediction benchmarks.'}, {'id': 'mem_038', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper introduces DimeNet, a graph neural network  
      that uses directional message passing with rotationally equivariant message embeddings and physically inspired spherical Bessel–harmonic basis         
      representations to explicitly model angular information, significantly outperforming prior methods on QM9 and MD17 benchmarks.'}, {'id': 'mem_039',    
      'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'TransPolymer is the first Transformer-based language model for polymer property prediction, featuring a              
      chemically-aware tokenizer and pretraining on 5M unlabeled polymer sequences via Masked Language Modeling, achieving state-of-the-art results on ten   
      benchmarks by effectively learning structure-property relationships from polymer sequences.'}, {'id': 'mem_040', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract':      
      'EquiformerV2 improves equivariant Transformers by integrating eSCN convolutions for efficient scaling to higher-degree representations and introducing
      three architectural enhancements—attention re-normalization, separable S² activation, and separable layer normalization—achieving state-of-the-art     
      accuracy on OC20 and OC22 with better speed-accuracy trade-offs and 2× reduction in DFT calculations for adsorption energy prediction.'}, {'id':       
      'mem_041', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper proposes a data-augmented graph convolutional neural network that accurately predicts polymer  
      glass transition temperatures from monomer structures and provides chemically interpretable insights to guide rational molecular design.'}, {'id':     
      'mem_042', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper proposes FGNN, a hybrid neural network that combines an enhanced graph attention network with a 
      novel feature selection algorithm (CNMIM) to jointly leverage molecular graphs and fingerprints for improved molecular property prediction,            
      demonstrating superior performance, noise robustness, and interpretability across multiple benchmarks.'}, {'id': 'mem_043', 'type': 'knowledge',       
      'abstract': 'The paper proposes Substructure-Mask Explanation (SME), a chemistry-intuitive method that explains graph neural network predictions by    
      attributing them to chemically meaningful substructures—such as BRICS fragments, Murcko scaffolds, and functional groups—enabling reliable,            
      interpretable, and actionable insights for molecular property prediction and structural optimization.'}, {'id': 'mem_044', 'type': 'knowledge',        
      'abstract': 'By leveraging natural language processing to extract data from over 3,300 papers, this work demonstrates that active learning strategies  
      could have accelerated the discovery of high-efficiency polymer solar cell donor–acceptor pairs by 75% (15 years) compared to historical               
      trial-and-error approaches.'}, {'id': 'mem_045', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper introduces polyBERT, a Transformer-based chemical language
      model that treats polymer SMILES strings as a language, enabling an end-to-end, ultrafast polymer informatics pipeline that matches the accuracy of    
      state-of-the-art handcrafted fingerprints while accelerating computation by over two orders of magnitude.'}, {'id': 'mem_046', 'type': 'knowledge',    
      'abstract': 'The paper introduces a Physics-Enforced Neural Network (PENN) that integrates empirical rheological equations into a neural architecture  
      to predict polymer melt viscosity from chemistry and processing conditions, achieving superior extrapolation and physical consistency compared to      
      physics-unaware machine learning models.'}, {'id': 'mem_047', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This Review presents an AI-driven, application-specific
      protocol for designing functional and sustainable polymers by integrating target property criteria, virtual generation of synthetically accessible     
      candidates, machine learning prediction, and experimental validation across energy and sustainability domains.'}, {'id': 'mem_048', 'type':            
      'knowledge', 'abstract': 'Prompt-MolOpt leverages prompt engineering in a transformer architecture to enable data-efficient, multiproperty molecular   
      optimization—even in zero-shot settings—by using property-specific embeddings to guide fragment modifications while optionally preserving              
      user-specified pharmacophores.'}, {'id': 'mem_049', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The authors present SPACIER, an open-source framework that       
      integrates fully automated all-atom classical molecular dynamics (via RadonPy) into Bayesian optimization pipelines for on-demand polymer design,      
      demonstrating its capability by discovering and synthesizing optical polymers that surpass the empirical Pareto frontier between refractive index and  
      Abbe number.'}, {'id': 'mem_050', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper extends Shapley values to explain predictive uncertainty by defining    
      information-theoretic characteristic functions based on conditional entropy and KL divergence, providing feature attributions for local uncertainty    
      with theoretical links to conditional independence and finite-sample error control via conformal inference.'}, {'id': 'mem_051', 'type': 'knowledge',  
      'abstract': 'The paper proposes KANO, a knowledge graph-enhanced molecular contrastive learning framework that uses an element-oriented knowledge graph
      to guide both pre-training (via element-guided graph augmentation) and fine-tuning (via functional prompts), achieving state-of-the-art performance and
      chemically sound interpretability on 14 molecular property prediction benchmarks.'}, {'id': 'mem_052', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper    
      introduces a periodic polymer graph representation that explicitly encodes polymer chain periodicity and combines it with a message-passing neural     
      network to automatically learn chemically relevant descriptors, achieving state-of-the-art accuracy on 8 out of 10 polymer property prediction         
      tasks.'}, {'id': 'mem_053', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper demonstrates that BigSMILES achieves polymer property prediction accuracy     
      comparable to SMILES while enabling faster model training and lower computational costs due to its more compact textual representation, establishing it
      as a practical and efficient alternative for polymer machine learning tasks.'}, {'id': 'mem_054', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper proposes
      Chem-DAGNN, a chemical-knowledge-based interpretable graph neural network that leverages small data by augmenting polyimide-specific datasets with     
      diverse polymer glass transition temperature data, enabling the rapid discovery and experimental validation of 89 novel polyimides with exceptional    
      heat resistance (Tg > 405°C, up to 450°C).'}, {'id': 'mem_055', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper introduces a Strongly Correlated Neural    
      Network (SCN) that represents molecular units as adaptive neural networks and uses a self-consistent feedback loop to model strong correlations,       
      enabling accurate forward structural prediction and one-to-many inverse design in the HP lattice protein model.'}, {'id': 'mem_056', 'type':           
      'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This Account presents a machine learning-assisted design framework for advanced polymeric materials, addressing data scarcity
      and multiscale structure–property complexity through novel representations (e.g., polymer fingerprints), multifidelity modeling, and high-throughput   
      virtual screening, thereby accelerating the discovery of high-performance polymers.'}, {'id': 'mem_057', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The authors 
      present RadonPy, an open-source Python library that automates all-atom classical molecular dynamics simulations to compute 15 thermophysical properties
      for over 1000 amorphous polymers, validates results against experiments, uses transfer learning to correct systematic biases, and identifies eight     
      polymers with high thermal conductivity (>0.4 W/m·K) along with their underlying mechanisms.'}, {'id': 'mem_058', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The
      paper introduces Joint Multi-domain Pre-training (JMP), a supervised pre-training strategy that trains a single model on 120M atomic systems from      
      diverse chemical domains, enabling state-of-the-art performance on 34 of 40 downstream tasks and demonstrating that large-scale, multi-domain          
      pre-training significantly improves generalization and scaling in atomic property prediction.'}, {'id': 'mem_059', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract':    
      'This paper presents DMPNN-MoE, a novel deep learning model integrating directed message passing neural networks with mixture-of-experts to accurately 
      predict temperature-dependent small-molecule solubility across diverse solute-solvent systems, achieving state-of-the-art performance and robust       
      generalization on a large curated dataset of 56,945 experimental measurements.'}, {'id': 'mem_060', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'Uni-Mol is the   
      first universal 3D molecular representation learning framework that pretrains SE(3)-equivariant Transformer models on 209M molecular conformations and 
      3M protein pockets, enabling state-of-the-art performance in both molecular property prediction and 3D spatial tasks like binding pose prediction and  
      conformation generation.'}, {'id': 'mem_061', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper introduces M3GNet, a universal graph deep learning           
