      up to three orders of magnitude fewer training samples than existing methods.'}, {'id': 'mem_063', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper         
      introduces a general class of material descriptors based on kernel mean embedding that preserves full distributional information of component features,
      enabling more accurate property prediction and guaranteed invertibility compared to conventional summary-statistic descriptors.'}, {'id': 'mem_064',   
      'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper introduces a de novo design framework for solid polymer electrolytes using GPT-based and diffusion-based  
      generative models, identifying 17 novel candidates with over 100% higher ionic conductivity than existing benchmarks through combined generative AI,   
      graph neural network screening, and molecular dynamics validation.'}, {'id': 'mem_065', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper proposes GEM, a    
      geometry-enhanced molecular representation learning method that integrates a dual-graph GNN architecture modeling atom-bond-angle relationships with   
      geometry-level self-supervised learning tasks, achieving state-of-the-art performance on 14 of 15 molecular property prediction benchmarks by          
      effectively leveraging 3D spatial structure.'}, {'id': 'mem_066', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper introduces evidential deep learning for 
      molecular property prediction, providing calibrated, single-shot epistemic uncertainty estimates without sampling, and demonstrates its utility in     
      improving sample efficiency via active learning and boosting experimental validation rates in virtual screening.'}, {'id': 'mem_067', 'type':          
      'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper presents Graphormer, a standard Transformer-based architecture enhanced with centrality, spatial, and edge        
      encodings that effectively incorporate graph structural information, achieving state-of-the-art results on multiple graph-level prediction benchmarks  
      including OGB-LSC.'}, {'id': 'mem_068', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This benchmark study systematically evaluates nine uncertainty quantification
      methods across diverse polymer property prediction tasks, revealing that optimal UQ strategy is highly context-dependent: Ensemble excels in general   
      prediction, BNN-MCMC in out-of-distribution scenarios, NGBoost for high-Tg polymers, and BNN-VI across diverse polymer classes.'}, {'id': 'mem_069',   
      'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper proposes eSEN, a smooth and conservative machine learning interatomic potential that passes energy         
      conservation tests in molecular dynamics, enabling strong correlation between test errors and physical property prediction performance, and achieving  
      state-of-the-art results in materials stability, thermal conductivity, and phonon calculations.'}, {'id': 'mem_070', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract':  
      'The paper introduces Attentive FP, a graph neural network architecture that uses a graph attention mechanism to achieve state-of-the-art predictive   
      performance on diverse molecular property datasets while providing interpretable insights into nonlocal intramolecular interactions.'}, {'id':         
      'mem_071', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper introduces polyGNN, a multitask graph neural network that learns polymer features directly from 
      repeat unit SMILES strings, achieving 1–2 orders of magnitude faster fingerprinting than handcrafted methods while maintaining comparable or better    
      accuracy across 30+ diverse polymer properties.'}, {'id': 'mem_072', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'The paper proposes Modof, a novel deep          
      generative model that optimizes molecules by learning to modify a single fragment at a predicted disconnection site, thereby preserving the core       
      scaffold and better aligning with real-world medicinal chemistry practices, and demonstrates its superior performance over state-of-the-art methods on 
      benchmark property optimization tasks.'}, {'id': 'mem_073', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'FragNet introduces a GNN architecture for molecular      
