      graph attention mechanisms, achieving SOTA on ESOL (RMSE 0.881), Clintox (AUC 86.8), and Sider (AUC 63.7) while enabling identification of             
      property-increasing/decreasing substructures.'}, {'id': 'mem_074', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper introduces polymer graph representation
      that explicitly captures periodicity by adding a periodic edge connecting terminal atoms of a trimer, achieving 20% average error reduction across 10  
      polymer properties compared to hand-designed molecular descriptors and demonstrating that MPNN-learned features correlate with chemically meaningful   
      descriptors.'}, {'id': 'mem_075', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'LSR-MP is a physics-informed message-passing framework that combines short-range   
      EGNN message passing with long-range bipartite atom-fragment interactions via BRICS fragmentation, achieving up to 40% MAE reduction on large          
      biomolecules while maintaining computational efficiency.'}, {'id': 'mem_076', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'PerioGT introduces a periodicity-aware 
      deep learning framework for polymers that incorporates chemical knowledge-driven periodicity priors through contrastive learning and prompt-guided     
      fine-tuning, achieving state-of-the-art performance on 16 downstream tasks and successfully identifying two antimicrobial polymers with potent activity
      against MRSA.'}, {'id': 'mem_078', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'SO3kRATEs is a Euclidean transformer for machine learned force fields that        
      overcomes the accuracy-stability-speed trade-off by replacing expensive SO(3) convolutions (O(l_max^6)) with a self-attention mechanism on invariant   
      projections (O(l_max²+F)), achieving ~30x speedup while maintaining MD stability through equivariant representations.'}, {'id': 'mem_079', 'type':     
      'knowledge', 'abstract': 'GRIN introduces repetition-invariant graph representations for polymers by combining max-aggregation GNNs (aligned with MST  
      construction) with repeat-unit augmentation, providing theoretical guarantees that 3 repeating units are minimal for optimal invariant learning.'},    
      {'id': 'mem_081', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'CELLI (Charge Equilibration Layer for Long-range Interactions) generalizes the classical Qeq method
      into a model-agnostic building block for equivariant GNN potentials, enabling modeling of long-range electrostatic interactions and charge transfer    
      while maintaining computational efficiency and interpretability through explicit charge predictions.'}, {'id': 'mem_082', 'type': 'knowledge',         
      'abstract': 'MBNN-att introduces atomic attention mechanism into many-body function corrected neural networks, achieving CPU-friendly linear scaling   
      O(N) while matching or exceeding GPU-based graph methods on energy properties (MAE ~5.3 meV on QM9), with attention weights physically interpretable as
      atomic orbital contributions.'}, {'id': 'mem_084', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'Day 3 Journal: Designed IAPT experiment integrating Days 1-3      
