      optimal for extensive properties and mean/max pooling preferred for intensive properties in extrapolation scenarios.'}, {'id': 'mem_089', 'type':      
      'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper develops Vivace, a fast SE(3)-equivariant MLFF for polymer simulations, introduces PolyArena benchmark (130       
      polymers with experimental densities and Tg), and PolyData training dataset, demonstrating that MLFFs trained purely on ab initio data can predict     
      experimental polymer bulk properties (density MAE 0.04 g/cm³, Tg MAE 43K), outperforming classical force fields.'}, {'id': 'mem_091', 'type':          
      'knowledge', 'abstract': 'TopicState: Research directions in polymer deep learning and active hypotheses regarding interpretable physics-inspired      
      neural network architectures. Currently restricted to existing polymer datasets, but leveraging validated hypotheses from other molecular deep learning
      tasks is permitted.'}, {'id': 'mem_092', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'GPIP proposes a geometry-enhanced self-supervised pretraining framework for 
      machine learning interatomic potentials (MLIPs) that leverages inexpensive classical molecular dynamics (CMD) data with three complementary SSL tasks  
      (masking, denoising, contrastive learning), achieving 10x data efficiency improvement with negligible computational cost compared to ab initio         
      calculations.'}, {'id': 'mem_093', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'MoCL introduces domain knowledge-aware contrastive learning for molecular graphs  
      via two innovations: (1) substructure substitution using bioisosteres (230 rules) for semantics-preserving augmentation, and (2) global contrast loss  
      using ECFP-derived molecular similarity to encode dataset structure, achieving state-of-the-art on 7 molecular benchmarks.'}, {'id': 'mem_094', 'type':
      'knowledge', 'abstract': 'GraphMAE introduces a masked graph autoencoder for self-supervised graph representation learning, addressing four key        
      deficiencies in prior GAEs: over-emphasis on structure reconstruction, lack of input corruption, MSE sensitivity, and weak decoders. By combining      
      masked feature reconstruction, scaled cosine error, re-mask decoding with GNN decoders, GraphMAE achieves SOTA results on 21 datasets across node      
      classification, graph classification, and transfer learning tasks.'}, {'id': 'mem_095', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper unifies three     
      fundamental GNN problems (vanishing gradients, over-smoothing, over-squashing) through a control theory lens, demonstrating that traditional GNNs      
      suffer from "extreme gradient vanishing" due to normalized adjacency contraction, and proposes GNN-SSM—a state-space model formulation that enables    
      direct Jacobian spectrum control for improved depth and long-range modeling.'}, {'id': 'mem_098', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'X2-GNN integrates  
      atomic orbital overlap integrals (S) and core Hamiltonians (H^core) as physics-informed features into an E(3)-invariant message passing GNN, achieving 
      strong generalization from small molecules (QM9, up to 9 heavy atoms) to large molecules (OCELOT, up to 75 heavy atoms) with consistent per-atom       
      errors, demonstrating that quantum chemical integrals provide transferable representations for molecular property prediction.'}, {'id': 'mem_099',     
      'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'KA-GNN introduces the first non-trivial integration of Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks into GNNs at three levels (node    
      embedding, message passing, readout), with Fourier series-based activation functions providing theoretical approximation guarantees and achieving      
      state-of-the-art on 7 molecular property prediction benchmarks.'}, {'id': 'mem_100', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper provides a unified   
      theoretical framework connecting vanishing gradients, over-smoothing, and over-squashing in GNNs through spectral analysis of layer-wise Jacobians, and
      proposes GNN-SSM, a state-space model formulation that enables direct control of gradient dynamics at no extra parameter cost.'}, {'id': 'mem_102',    
      'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'TopicState: Research directions in polymer deep learning and active hypotheses regarding interpretable               
      physics-inspired neural network architectures. Day 6: PolyKAN-SSM failed to beat SOTA (38.17 vs 30.8). Fourier-KAN helped slightly, GNN-SSM too        
      restrictive, periodicity-aware architecture is key missing piece.'}, {'id': 'mem_103', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'This paper introduces a       
      periodic polymer graph representation that explicitly captures polymer periodicity by adding a bond between terminal atoms of a trimer, combined with  
      MPNN to learn polymer-specific descriptors. Across 10 polymer properties (15,219 data points), the polymer graph achieves 20% average error reduction  
      vs monomer-based representations, with Tg RMSE improving from 41.39K to 34.91K.'}, {'id': 'mem_104', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'CTGNN combines  
      Transformer architectures with graph neural networks for crystal property prediction, using dual-Transformer layers (intra-crystal for atom features,  
      inter-atomic for edge features) and angular encoding to capture both local and global structural information, achieving significant improvements on    
      formation energy and bandgap prediction.'}, {'id': 'mem_105', 'type': 'knowledge', 'abstract': 'DenseGNN proposes a universal and scalable GNN         
      architecture combining Dense Connectivity Networks (DCN), hierarchical node-edge graph residual networks (HRN), and Local Structure Order Parameters   
      Embedding (LOPE) to overcome over-smoothing, enable very deep GNNs, and efficiently capture many-body interactions without expensive nested graph      
      networks, achieving SOTA on Matbench, JARVIS-DFT, QM9, and other benchmarks.'}]}                                                                       
